					"text": "param angle 0"
				}
			},
			{
				"box": {
					"code": "/*\r\n * sr.motion.genjit\r\n *\r\n * Directional motion blur effect\r\n * Part of SevenRad Max 8 Effects\r\n *\r\n * Parameters:\r\n *   kernel_size (int 1-100): Blur length in pixels\r\n *   angle (float 0-360): Direction in degrees\r\n *                        0=right, 90=up, 180=left, 270=down\r\n *\r\n * Algorithm:\r\n *   - Samples along a line in the specified direction\r\n *   - Uniform weighting (box blur)\r\n *   - Centered on current pixel (samples from -half to +half)\r\n *\r\n * Coordinate System:\r\n *   - Angle 0 = positive X (right)\r\n *   - Angle increases counter-clockwise\r\n *   - Y coordinate negated because screen Y increases downward\r\n *\r\n * Visual Effect:\r\n *   Creates camera motion blur or speed lines effect.\r\n *   Simulates camera/object movement in specified direction.\r\n *\r\n * Source: src/sevenrad_stills/operations/motion_blur_taichi.py\r\n */\r\n\r\n\r\n// Convert angle to radians\r\nrad = angle * 3.14159265359 / 180.0;\r\n\r\n// Calculate direction vector in normalized coordinates\r\n// dx: horizontal component (cos for 0=right)\r\n// dy: vertical component (negative sin because Y increases downward)\r\ndx = cos(rad) / dim.x;\r\ndy = -sin(rad) / dim.y;\r\n\r\n// Accumulator for color sum\r\nsum = vec(0, 0, 0, 0);\r\n\r\n// Calculate half-length for centered blur\r\nhalf = float(kernel_size - 1) / 2.0;\r\n\r\n// Sample along the motion direction\r\nfor (i = 0; i < kernel_size; i += 1) {\r\n    // Position along blur line, centered on current pixel\r\n    t = float(i) - half;\r\n\r\n    // Calculate offset in normalized coordinates\r\n    offset = vec(t * dx, t * dy);\r\n\r\n    // Sample and accumulate\r\n    sum += sample(in1, norm + offset);\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Average all samples (uniform weighting)\r\nout1 = sum / float(kernel_size);",
					"fontname": "Arial",
					"fontsize": 12.0,
					"id": "obj-4",
					"maxclass": "codebox",
					"numinlets": 1,
					"numoutlets": 1,
					"outlettype": [
